Good, mypy is installed. Now I need to create the git pre-commit hook that runs mypy on all Python files in src/ and blocks the commit if type-checking fails.

The pre-commit hook should:
1. Run mypy on all Python files in src/
2. Check if mypy exits with a non-zero exit code
3. If it fails, block the commit by exiting with a non-zero exit code

Let me create the pre-commit hook script:
======================================================================

======================================================================
                              TOOL CALL                               
======================================================================
Function: execute_command
Arguments: {"command": "cat > .git/hooks/pre-commit << 'EOF'\n#!/bin/bash\n# Run mypy on all Python files in src/\necho \"Running mypy type checking...\"\nmypy src/\n\n# If mypy failed, block the commit\nif [ $? -ne 0 ]; then\n    echo \"Type-checking failed. Commit blocked.\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"Type-checking passed.\"\nEOF"}
